@baseUrl = https://server.velaroqa.com
@productId = 1

### Create an order (requires an existing product_id)
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": {{productId}},
  "quantity": 2,
  "total_price": 200.00,
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "maroufulislam.zishan@gmail.com",
  "phone": "+1 555 0100",
  "delivery_address": "123 Main Street"
}

### Get all orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
# If ADMIN_TOKEN is configured in .env, add:
# Authorization: Bearer your-admin-token

### Confirm the order created above
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
# If ADMIN_TOKEN is configured in .env, add:
# Authorization: Bearer your-admin-token

{
  "status": "confirmed"
}

### Decline the order created above
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
# If ADMIN_TOKEN is configured in .env, add:
# Authorization: Bearer your-admin-token

{
  "status": "declined"
}

### Invalid status (expected 400 Bad Request)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.$.id}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
# If ADMIN_TOKEN is configured in .env, add:
# Authorization: Bearer your-admin-token

{
  "status": "shipped"
}

### 1. Create a Product (POST with multiple image uploads)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=MyBoundary

--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

Classic shoes
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="price"

29.99
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="discount"

10.00
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Comfortable and stylish athletic shoes.
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="sizes"

[40, 42, 44]
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="shoes1.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./shirt.jpg
--MyBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="images"; filename="shoes2.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./shoes2.jpg
--MyBoundary--


### 2. Get All Products (GET with Optional Filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/4

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### put {{baseUrl}}/api/products/4
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/4 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="discount"

10.00
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--


###
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/3